A||N||7||foxgapfiero||I'm building a Fiero trailer||||1||
Z||000000||foxgapfiero||11-07-2001||05:51 PM||||I'd like to start mailing to anyone that has a Fiero trailer. I'm just about ready to cut this thing in half and I have a few questions that need opinions on. Even if you didn't build the trailer yourself, please reply. Skitime sent me some great pictures awhile back, but the more I get the better this trailer will be.    Thanks to all.<P>------------------<BR>Mark Hoagland<BR>86GT 3.4<BR>88GT T-Top<BR>85GT caddy v-8 next swap<BR>84SE trailer next project||||reg||1
Z||000001||stsmithgt||11-07-2001||06:49 PM|||| <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/trailer_fiero_1.jpg">  I grabbed this of the forum awhile back.  It's an interesting design not quite cut in half.  Thought it might add to your creative gears turning in your head. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>------------------<BR>My work of art 4..s..money. <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/4money.jpg"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||MinnGreenGT||11-07-2001||07:40 PM||||The one shown above was built by David Gageby in Minnesota (his number may still be on the Minnesota Fieros Forever website).  Look him up and give him a call- he'd be glad to tell you his experiences.  <P>I've been collecting parts for a GT-style trailer as well (too much stuff to carry to long distance shows  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">).  So I'm curious about what others have done as well.  Also, I'm wondering if anyone has info on the "hidden" style trailer hitch from a few years back.  I saw one that was mounted behind the liscense plate and hinged up to insert the ball hitch.<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
Z||000003||Dragon||11-07-2001||10:32 PM||||We sat down one day and cut a coupe in half.  I did not have papers on the car so it was no good.  It really gets the people looking when you fly down the interstate with half a Fiero following along<P>Look behind the coupe on the signature picture<P>I did find a picture of the trailer after we cut it standing on the firewall<BR> <A HREF="http://floridafieros.org/daytona2002" TARGET=_blank>http://floridafieros.org/daytona2002</A> <P>------------------<BR>Dragon<BR>       <IMG SRC="http://SpaceCoastFieros.com/dragonfamily.jpg">       <BR>   Space Coast Fieros -&gt; Florida Fiero Council||||reg||6
Z||000004||GarethWright||11-07-2001||10:51 PM||||Another shot of Davids trailer courtesy of the "MODS" Gallery<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/gallery/Mods/Dave_Gageby_trailerj.jpg">  <BR>I have been thinking of doing a GT style trailer myself, but as Mom says "not while you're living here!" It will have to be put off for a while.  I was going to use the rear clip, 1/4 panels, and bumber to either modify an existing flatbed trailer, or custom-build a frame chassis, mainly because I don't really want to completely destroy a fastback Fiero  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif">  Also, I wasn't going to use the rear window glass, and leave the top of the clip as a wing sort of thing.  <p>[This message has been edited by GarethWright (edited 11-07-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000005||FieroMontreal||11-07-2001||10:51 PM||||Talk about a weekend project! lol<P>I love the one in that Pic up there.. but what if it rains? wouldnt the seats get wet?<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/sigfieromontreal_1.gif"> <BR>1986 Fiero GT, STOCK Wingless, <BR>-Alex President of FieroMontreal... <A HREF="http://www.fieromontreal.com" TARGET=_blank>www.fieromontreal.com</A> ||||reg||1
